		"nodes": {
			"1": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "choice",
						"value": "Left"
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": true
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "number",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "text",
						"value": "STATIC\nThe Static node allows for the creation of static noise. This noise can be either colored, grayscale or two-tone. The mode can be adjusted in the inspector.\n\n- Patch Explained -\n\n• The Static needs to be fed some kind of changing signal to know that it is running.\n• In this Example we’re using a Saw Oscillator.\n• The Static nodes are sent to the crop nodes where they are cropped so all three examples fit on your screen.\n• The Video Mixer combines the Static nodes into one Output."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 219.7906494140625,
					"width": 927,
					"x": 120.41182708740234375,
					"y": -40.9039306640625
